{"toolCallId":"call_7a967ce1f8124e9cab1591163e3e05c8","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"---\ntitle: Spec Authoring Card\ndescription: The short path a model follows to write one spec packet that passes strict validation with no unfilled tokens.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"spec authoring card\"\n  - \"write a spec packet\"\n  - \"spec folder authoring steps\"\n  - \"fill a spec scaffold\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.0.3.0\n---\n\n# Spec Authoring Card\n\nThis card is the short path. Follow the steps in order. Each step has one action, one acceptance line and one command. When the command prints what the acceptance line says, go to the next step.\n\n`references/templates/template-guide.md` is the long guide. Read it only when a section's fill note leaves you unsure what to write.\n\n## 1. BOUNDS\n\nYou write one packet, in one folder. The folder is the one `create.sh` prints.\n\nAllowed writes: the packet folder and its `scratch/` folder.\nForbidden: `git commit`, `git push`, `git checkout`, `git switch`, `git branch`, `git reset`, `git stash`, `generate-context.js`, `/speckit:save`. Do not edit `.skilled/`, another packet or a source file. Do not run `create.sh` twice.\n\nAcceptance: you can name the packet folder and the one command you will run to check it.\nVerify: `pwd` prints the repository root, and `ls <packet folder>` lists `spec.md`.\n\n## 2. PICK THE LEVEL\n\nRun the level helper first.\n\n```bash\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --loc <lines> --files <count>\n```\n\nUse the level it prints. If it prints Level 0, use `--level 1`. Do not raise the level yourself. The level decides which files the packet needs.\n\n| Level | Files the packet needs |\n|-------|------------------------|\n| 1 | `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, and `implementation-summary.md` once implementation starts |\n| 2 | the Level 1 files plus `acceptance-criteria.md` |\n| 3 | the Level 2 files plus the architecture sections and a decision record when one is written |\n\nAcceptance: the level in the scaffold header matches the level the helper printed.\nVerify: `rg -n 'SPECKIT_LEVEL' <packet folder>/spec.md` prints one line with that level.\n\n## 3. SCAFFOLD\n\nCreate the packet with one command. Keep `--skip-branch` so no git state changes.\n\n```bash\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh --skip-branch --with-goal --level <level> --track <track> --short-name <two-to-four-words> \"<one sentence>\"\n```\n\nThe command prints the folder it made. Use that path for every later command. When `specs/<track>/graph-metadata.json` exists, `create.sh` also adds the packet to its `children_ids`. That write is the script's, not yours.\n\nAcceptance: the folder holds `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `scratch/`.\nVerify: `ls <packet folder>` lists those names.\n\n## 4. READ BEFORE YOU WRITE\n\nOpen one rendered example at the same level under `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/examples/level-<level>/`. Read `spec.md` and `tasks.md`.\n\nDo not copy from a `.tmpl` file. A `.tmpl` file carries tokens and gate markers. The examples are filled and safe to imitate for section shape, not for content.\n\nEach section of your scaffold carries a fill note. The note says what that section needs. Read the note before you write the section. The note is the contract for that section.\n\nAcceptance: you can say, in one sentence, what the first section of `spec.md` must contain.\nVerify: `sed -n '1,40p' <packet folder>/spec.md` shows the fill notes.\n\n## 5. ONE ACTION PER SECTION\n\nEach section does one job. Write one idea per paragraph. Do not repeat the same fact in two sections.\n\n- `spec.md` states the problem, the scope, the requirements and the success criteria.\n- `plan.md` states the approach, the files to change, the test plan and the dependencies.\n- `tasks.md` states the ordered actions.\n- `implementation-summary.md` states what changed and how it was checked. Write it last.\n\nDo not put a task list in `spec.md`. Do not put requirements in `plan.md`.\n\nAcceptance: every heading in the packet has content under it, and no heading holds content that belongs to another heading.\nVerify: `rg -n '^## ' <packet folder>/spec.md <packet folder>/plan.md` lists the headings you filled.\n\n## 6. THE PLAN SHAPE\n\nA plan has 3 or 4 steps. More than 4 steps means the feature is too large for one packet. Stop and ask, as section 11 says.\n\nEach step carries three lines:\n1. What the step does.\n2. The acceptance line: what is true when the step is done.\n3. The verify command: the command a reader runs, and the text it prints.\n\n```markdown\n### Step 1: Add the flag parser\n\nAcceptance: `--quiet` is accepted and the default output is unchanged.\nVerify: `bash script.sh --quiet` prints one line.\n```\n\nAcceptance: `plan.md` holds 3 or 4 steps, and each step has an acceptance line and a verify command.\nVerify: `rg -c '^### Step ' <packet folder>/plan.md` prints 3 or 4.\n\n## 7. TASK LINES\n\nEvery task line has one action, one file and one verify clause.\n\n```markdown\n- [ ] T001 Add the quiet flag to the option parser (`runtime/cli/spec/script.sh`). Verify: `bash runtime/cli/spec/script.sh --quiet` prints one line.\n```\n\nRules:\n- One action per task.\n- Name the file in parentheses.\n- End with `Verify:` and the command plus its expected output.\n- Put the tasks in the order you will run them.\n- Mark a task `[x]` only after its verify command printed the expected output.\n\nAcceptance: every task line, open or done, ends with a `Verify:` clause.\nVerify: `rg -c '^- \\[[ xB]\\] T[0-9].*Verify: ' <packet folder>/tasks.md` and `rg -c '^- \\[[ xB]\\] T[0-9]' <packet folder>/tasks.md` print the same number.\n\n## 8. FILL EVERY TOKEN\n\nA scaffold stamped `v2.3` or later carries tokens. A token starts with `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE:` and ends at the next closing bracket. Replace the whole token, brackets included, with real content. Do not leave a token in a finished packet.\n\nIf you cannot answer a question the token asks, write `UNKNOWN` in its place and write an open question in `goal.md` section 4.\n\nA token in a packet whose `spec.md` says `Status: Draft` is a warning, so strict validation can pass with tokens still in the file. A token in any other status is an error. Do not use the warning as permission. Count the tokens.\n\nAcceptance: the count is 0.\nVerify: `rg -o '\\[YOUR_VALUE_HERE:' <packet folder>/*.md | wc -l` prints 0.\n\n## 9. VALIDATE\n\nRun the validator once, after your last edit, before you claim the packet is done.\n\n```bash\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <packet folder> --strict --quiet\n```\n\nIt prints one `RESULT:` line per packet; the first line is the folder you named, and that line decides. `RESULT: PASSED (errors=0 ...)` is the pass. Do not run it again to re-check a pass.\n\nWhen it prints `FAILED`, run the same command once without `--quiet` and read every failing rule. Fix all of them in one pass, then run the `--quiet` command again. That is one round. Stop after three rounds and write the rules and their errors in the packet's `goal.md`.\n\nWhen the full output contains a `repair-derived.cjs ... --apply` command, run that command, then run the `--quiet` command again. It rewrites generated metadata, frontmatter packet pointers and the Spec Folder row, never your prose.\n\nAcceptance: the `--quiet` command prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\nVerify: the last `--quiet` run printed `RESULT: PASSED`.\n\n## 10. CLOSE\n\nA packet is closeable when:\n- every required file exists for its level\n- every token is filled, or replaced with `UNKNOWN` and an open question in `goal.md`\n- `tasks.md` has no `[B]` line\n- `implementation-summary.md` names the files that changed\n- the section 9 `--quiet` run printed `RESULT: PASSED`\n\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w5963e3680a/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"071fc7","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_7bb5ae8e30ba428eb7bcacc8e64a6b99","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"| REQ-008 | Duplicate email registration prevented |\n| REQ-009 | Users can log out |\n\n\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: User can complete full registration and login flow in under 30 seconds\n- **SC-002**: Authentication state persists correctly across browser refresh\n- **SC-003**: All security checklist items pass verification\n- **SC-004**: Test coverage > 80% for auth modules\n\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | bcrypt library | Cannot hash passwords | Use native crypto as fallback |\n| Dependency | jsonwebtoken | Cannot generate sessions | Session-based auth fallback |\n| Dependency | Database connection | Cannot store users | Validate DB connection at startup |\n| Risk | Token security | Session hijacking | HttpOnly cookies in Phase 2 |\n| Risk | Timing attacks | Email enumeration | Constant-time comparison |\n\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n---\n\n## 7. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n### Performance\n- **NFR-P01**: Login response time < 500ms (including bcrypt verification)\n- **NFR-P02**: Registration response time < 1000ms (including hash generation)\n- **NFR-P03**: Token validation < 10ms per request\n\n### Security\n- **NFR-S01**: Passwords hashed with bcrypt (cost factor 10+)\n- **NFR-S02**: No sensitive data in error messages (no credential enumeration)\n- **NFR-S03**: Input sanitized before database operations\n- **NFR-S04**: JWT secrets stored in environment variables only\n\n### Reliability\n- **NFR-R01**: Auth service available when database is reachable\n- **NFR-R02**: Graceful degradation with clear error messages on failures\n- **NFR-R03**: No data loss on service restart (stateless auth)\n\n\n---\n\n## 8. EDGE CASES\n\n### Data Boundaries\n- **Empty input**: Form validation prevents submission, inline error shown\n- **Maximum length**: Email capped at 255 chars, password at 128 chars\n- **Special characters**: Email validated against RFC 5322, password allows all printable ASCII\n- **Unicode**: Email normalized (lowercase), password preserved as-is\n\n### Error Scenarios\n- **Database connection failure**: Generic \"Service unavailable\" error, retry guidance\n- **Duplicate email**: Clear message \"An account with this email already exists\"\n- **Invalid token format**: Redirect to login with \"Session expired\" message\n- **Expired token**: Same handling as invalid token\n\n### Concurrent Operations\n- **Multiple login attempts**: Allow all (rate limiting in Phase 2)\n- **Simultaneous registration**: Database unique constraint prevents duplicates\n\n\n---\n\n## 9. RISK MATRIX\n\n| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation |\n|---------|-------------|--------|------------|------------|\n| R-001 | JWT secret compromised | H | L | Rotate secrets, short expiry |\n| R-002 | bcrypt vulnerability discovered | H | L | Monitor CVEs, update promptly |\n| R-003 | XSS extracts localStorage token | M | M | Migrate to HttpOnly cookies (Phase 2) |\n| R-004 | Brute force login attempts | M | H | Add rate limiting (Phase 2) |\n| R-005 | Database breach exposes hashes | M | L | bcrypt makes cracking expensive |\n\n\n---\n\n## 10. USER STORIES\n\n### US-001: New User Registration (Priority: P0)\n\n**As a** new visitor, **I want** to create an account with my email and password, **so that** I can access personalized features.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n1. Given I am on the registration page, When I enter a valid email and password (8+ chars), Then my account is created and I see a success message\n2. Given I try to register with an existing email, When I submit the form, Then I see \"An account with this email already exists\"\n3. Given I enter an invalid email format, When I submit the form, Then I see \"Please enter a valid email address\"\n\n### US-002: Returning User Login (Priority: P0)\n\n**As a** registered user, **I want** to log in with my credentials, **so that** I can access my account.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n1. Given I enter valid credentials, When I click login, Then I am redirected to the dashboard with my session active\n2. Given I enter invalid credentials, When I click login, Then I see \"Invalid email or password\"\n3. Given I close and reopen my browser, When I return within 24 hours, Then I am still logged in\n\n### US-003: User Logout (Priority: P1)\n\n**As a** logged-in user, **I want** to log out of my account, **so that** I can secure my session on shared devices.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n1. Given I am logged in, When I click logout, Then my session is terminated and I am redirected to the login page\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 11. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- Should we implement \"Remember Me\" functionality in this phase? **RESOLVED: Deferred to Phase 2**\n- What should the session token expiration time be? **RESOLVED: 24 hours**\n- Should we support concurrent sessions? **RESOLVED: Yes, no limit initially**\n\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n---\n\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n- **Implementation Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Task Breakdown**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Verification Checklist**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Decision Records**: See `decision-record.md`\n\n\n---\n\n<!--\nLEVEL 3 SPEC (~200 lines)\n- Core + L2 + L3 addendums\n- Executive summary, risk matrix, user stories\n- Full architecture documentation\n-->\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w5963e3680a/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"e4995f","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_7d7cab6e4fb34b67bb61cb81d23cb45d","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"--loc 300 --files 9 => Recommended Level: 1 (Baseline)\n--loc 400 --files 12 => Recommended Level: 1 (Baseline)\n--loc 250 --files 8 --api => Recommended Level: 1 (Baseline)\n--loc 350 --files 10 --db => Recommended Level: 1 (Baseline)\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w5963e3680a/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"e2c316","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_800c8ff3340a4a55979ef413594f931c","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add User Authentication\"\ndescription: \"Level 3 task list example with dependencies, milestone mapping and detailed verification tasks.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"task breakdown\"\n  - \"implementation tasks\"\n  - \"verification checklist\"\n  - \"user authentication\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n# Tasks: Add User Authentication\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core + level2-verify + level3-arch | v2.2 -->\n\n<!-- EXAMPLE: This is a filled-in Level 3 task list with comprehensive tracking\nincluding dependencies, milestone mapping, and detailed verification tasks. -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path) [effort] {deps: T###}. Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n---\n\n## Milestone Reference\n\n| Milestone | Tasks | Target |\n|-----------|-------|--------|\n| M1 | T001-T006 | Day 1 EOD |\n| M2 | T007-T012 | Day 2 EOD |\n| M3 | T013-T022 | Day 3 EOD |\n| M4 | T023-T028 | Day 4 noon |\n| M5 | T029-T042 | Day 5 EOD |\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup [Milestone M1]\n\n- [x] T001 Create auth directory structure (`src/auth/`) [15m]. Verify: `ls src/auth` exits 0.\n- [x] T002 Install bcrypt, jsonwebtoken, express-validator (`package.json`) [10m]. Verify: `npm ls bcrypt jsonwebtoken` prints both versions.\n- [x] T003 [P] Configure environment variables (`env.example`, `.env`) [15m]. Verify: `rg -c JWT_SECRET env.example` prints 1.\n- [x] T004 [P] Add User model to Prisma schema (`prisma/schema.prisma`) [20m]. Verify: `npx prisma validate` prints that the schema is valid.\n\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Database [Milestone M1]\n\n- [x] T005 Run Prisma migration (`prisma/migrations/`) [15m] {deps: T004}. Verify: `npx prisma migrate status` prints \"Database schema is up to date\".\n- [x] T006 Add unique index on email (`prisma/schema.prisma`) [10m] {deps: T005}. Verify: `rg -n '@unique' prisma/schema.prisma` prints the email line.\n\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Core Services [Milestone M2]\n\n### Hash Service\n- [x] T007 Implement hashPassword function (`src/utils/hash.js`) [30m] {deps: T002}. Verify: `node --check src/utils/hash.js` exits 0.\n- [x] T008 Implement verifyPassword function (`src/utils/hash.js`) [20m] {deps: T007}. Verify: `node --check src/utils/hash.js` exits 0.\n\n### Token Service\n- [x] T009 [P] Implement generateToken function (`src/utils/token.js`) [30m] {deps: T002}. Verify: `node --check src/utils/token.js` exits 0.\n- [x] T010 [P] Implement verifyToken function (`src/utils/token.js`) [30m] {deps: T009}. Verify: `node --check src/utils/token.js` exits 0.\n\n### Validators\n- [x] T011 [P] Create registration validator (`src/validators/auth.js`) [30m] {deps: T002}. Verify: `node --check src/validators/auth.js` exits 0.\n- [x] T012 [P] Create login validator (`src/validators/auth.js`) [20m] {deps: T011}. Verify: `node --check src/validators/auth.js` exits 0.\n\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-4 -->\n## Phase 4: API Endpoints [Milestone M3]\n\n### Registration\n- [x] T013 Create registration route handler (`src/auth/register.js`) [45m] {deps: T007, T011}. Verify: `curl -si -X POST localhost:3000/auth/register` prints `HTTP/1.1 400`.\n- [x] T014 Add user creation with hashed password (`src/auth/register.js`) [30m] {deps: T013}. Verify: `node --check src/auth/register.js` exits 0.\n- [x] T015 Add duplicate email check (`src/auth/register.js`) [20m] {deps: T014}. Verify: `node --check src/auth/register.js` exits 0.\n\n### Login\n- [x] T016 Create login route handler (`src/auth/login.js`) [30m] {deps: T008, T009, T012}. Verify: `curl -si -X POST localhost:3000/auth/login` prints `HTTP/1.1 400`.\n- [x] T017 Add password verification (`src/auth/login.js`) [20m] {deps: T016}. Verify: `node --check src/auth/login.js` exits 0.\n- [x] T018 Add token generation on success (`src/auth/login.js`) [20m] {deps: T017}. Verify: `node --check src/auth/login.js` exits 0.\n\n### Logout\n- [x] T019 Create logout route handler (`src/auth/logout.js`) [20m] {deps: T010}. Verify: `node --check src/auth/logout.js` exits 0.\n\n### Middleware\n- [x] T020 Create auth middleware (`src/middleware/auth.js`) [45m] {deps: T010}. Verify: `node --check src/middleware/auth.js` exits 0.\n- [x] T021 Add protected route example (`src/routes/dashboard.js`) [15m] {deps: T020}. Verify: `curl -si localhost:3000/dashboard` prints `HTTP/1.1 401`.\n\n### Integration\n- [x] T022 Wire up all routes in app.js (`app.js`) [20m] {deps: T015, T018, T019, T020}. Verify: `curl -si localhost:3000/dashboard` prints `HTTP/1.1 401`.\n\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-4 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-5 -->\n## Phase 5: UI [Milestone M4]\n=====AC=====\n---\ntitle: \"Acceptance Criteria: User Authentication\"\ndescription: \"The criteria this packet must satisfy before it may be closed, each one met, waived by a decision record, or superseded by one.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"acceptance criteria\"\n  - \"closure gate\"\n  - \"ac traceability\"\n  - \"waiver adr\"\nimportance_tier: \"important\"\ncontextType: \"implementation\"\n---\n# Acceptance Criteria: User Authentication\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: acceptance-criteria | v2.2 -->\n<!-- HVR_REFERENCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-with-human-voice/references/hvr-rules.md -->\n\n> This document decides whether the packet may close. A packet is closeable when\n> every row below is `Met`, `Waived` or `Superseded`. A `Waived` or `Superseded`\n> row MUST name an ADR that exists in `decision-record.md`.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n**Packet:** examples/level-3\n**Level:** 3\n**Status:** Complete\n**Date:** 2026-08-29\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:criteria -->\n## 2. CRITERIA\n\nOne row per criterion. `AC-ID` is stable once written: supersede a criterion, never renumber it.\n\n| AC-ID | REQ | Given / When / Then | Verification | Status | Waiver |\n|-------|-----|---------------------|--------------|--------|--------|\n| AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given a visitor on the registration form, When they submit a valid email and password, Then a user row exists and a success message is shown | `tests/auth/register.test.ts:24` | Met | - |\n| AC-002 | REQ-002 | Given a registered user, When they submit valid credentials, Then a token is issued and they land on the dashboard | `tests/auth/login.test.ts:31` | Met | - |\n| AC-003 | REQ-003 | Given a registration request, When the password is persisted, Then only a bcrypt hash of 10 rounds is stored | `tests/auth/hash.test.ts:12` | Met | - |\n| AC-004 | REQ-004 | Given malformed input, When the form is submitted, Then the email format and the 8-character minimum are enforced | `tests/auth/validation.test.ts:18` | Met | - |\n| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given a request without a valid token, When a protected route is called, Then the API returns 401 | `tests/auth/guard.test.ts:9` | Met | - |\n| AC-006 | REQ-006 | Given a completed build, When the security review runs, Then the security team records sign-off | Security review record | Met | - |\n| AC-007 | REQ-007 | Given an invalid login, When the error renders, Then it is generic and does not enumerate credentials | `tests/auth/login.test.ts:57` | Met | - |\n\n### Status values\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n|-------|---------|\n| `Met` | Verified. The Verification cell names evidence that was actually observed. |\n| `Unmet` | Not yet satisfied. Blocks closure. |\n| `Waived` | Deliberately not pursued. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n| `Superseded` | Replaced by a different criterion or decision. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n\n### Waiver cell\n\nWrite `-` when the row is `Met` or `Unmet`. Write `ADR-NNN` when the row is\n`Waived` or `Superseded`, naming a decision record that exists in\n`decision-record.md`. A waiver naming an ADR that is not there fails validation:\nthe point of a waiver is that someone recorded the reasoning, so an unbacked\nwaiver is treated as an unmet criterion rather than as a pass.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:closure -->\n## 3. CLOSURE STATEMENT\n\n**Closeable:** Yes\n\nEvery criterion is met with a cited test. Nothing was waived, so the decision record carries no closure ADR.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:closure -->\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w5963e3680a/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"029e0d","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
